<item>
            <title>[LU-20454] gid2name and uid2name may return invalid name</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20454</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;gid2name() in lustre/utils/lfs.c returns unprintable group name. &#160;gid2name() calls getgrgid_r,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;whose prototype is &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;int getgrgid_r(gid_t gid, struct group *restrict grp,&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; char buf&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;restrict .buflen&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, size_t buflen,&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; struct group **restrict result);&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In gid2name, it is assumed that group name is stored at &amp;amp;buf&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, that is not guaranteed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;uid2name may have the same problem.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;a href=&apos;mailto:root@vhost31&apos;&gt;root@vhost31&lt;/a&gt;:~# lsb_release -a&lt;br/&gt;
